        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/DK-arcade-art.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Lego and Nintendo's collaborations have been among the most eye-catching and sought-after in recent years. From <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/super-mario-wonder-captain-toad-and-wario-sets-join-nintendo-lego-range\">little Super Mario builds</a>, to a near-perfect <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/lego-game-boy-pre-order-nintendo\">replica of the original Game Boy</a>, to <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/lego-pokemon-unveiled-but-catching-em-all-will-cost-you\">complex Pok&eacute;mon sets</a>, collectors are clearly lapping up the 'brickified' versions of Nintendo icons. And perhaps the most ambitious one may be around the corner.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/lego-donkey-kong-arcade-machine-set-leaked\">Read more</a></p>",
